wOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":6,"created_at":"2026-01-17T23:05:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T16:31:03Z","closed_at":"2026-01-18T16:28:42Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Found in v4.6.rc.custom_build [741fb8a30]\n- Issue exists in 4.5.1-stable and 4.0\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.rc (741fb8a30) - EndeavourOS #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun, 11 Jan 2026 17:10:53 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7900 XTX (RADV NAVI31) - AMD Ryzen 7 9800X3D 8-Core Processor (8 threads) - 91.93 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen attempting to use the `self` keyword specifically in `_notification()` inside of an inner class, it is null and no functions from the inner class can be used.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOn a Node2D:\n\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nclass Test extends RefCounted:\n\tfunc _init() -> void:\n\t\tprint(self)\n\t\n\tfunc _notification(what: int) -> void:\n\t\tprint(self)\n\t\t#get_reference_count()\n\nvar test: Test\n\nfunc _init() -> void:\n\ttest = Test.new()\n\ttest = null\n\nfunc _notification(what: int) -> void:\n\tprint(self)\n```\n\nThe notifications for the Node2D script will print as expected, but `Test`'s will be null. If you uncomment `get_reference_count`, a runtime error will be thrown since it cannot call the function on a null value.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24692544/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"l